@thagomizerrr In wars of attrition, the front line shouldn't move. Instead, manpower metrics move.

When one side runs out of manpower, the front line disappears and the winner captures everything at once, unopposed.

For example, this happened to Germany in WW2. They lost not because the front line was slowly moving somewhere, but because they ran out of manpower.
